# The public sections. Each of these is a panel that slides over the home
# document — the gallery overlay and the community page — and js/routes.js is
# what opens the right one for the path. Without a fallback here Pages has no
# asset at /marketplace and answers its own 404, so the url in the sitemap, the
# link in the footer and the address the app itself writes would all be dead on
# a direct hit or a refresh. Exact paths, listed before the splats below so
# there is no question which rule answers.
#
# Keep this list, the ROUTES table in js/routes.js, the SECTIONS table in
# functions/_middleware.js and the cache rules in _headers in step.
/explore      /index.html  200
/marketplace  /index.html  200
/resources    /index.html  200
/blog         /index.html  200
/community    /index.html  200

# One url per destination. The bottom nav calls this section Gallery and the
# hero calls it Explore; /explore is the one that is canonical, indexed and in
# the sitemap, so the other name redirects into it rather than becoming a
# second address for the same grid.
/gallery      /explore     301

# spa fallback for artwork urls
/artwork/*  /index.html  200

# and for profiles, which js/profile.js pushes and functions/sitemap.xml.js
# publishes one of per member. This rule was missing while every other part of
# the system assumed it: _headers carries a /profile/* cache rule,
# functions/_middleware.js builds the Open Graph card for one, and
# js/startup.js opens the profile named in the path on boot. Without it Pages
# has no asset at that path and answers its own 404 — so every profile link
# ever shared, and every profile url in the sitemap, was dead.
/profile/*  /index.html  200

# the sign-in sheet writes /login while it is open (js/auth.js), so a refresh
# with it up has to reach the app rather than 404
/login      /index.html  200

# and for the four sections, which have their own links now — the viewer
# writes /resource/<id>, /blog/<id>, /listing/<id> and /job/<id> while an item
# is open, so those paths have to reach the app rather than 404
/resource/*  /index.html  200
/blog/*      /index.html  200
/listing/*   /index.html  200
/job/*       /index.html  200

# sitemap and robots.txt are not covered above
